\chapter{The D Toolkit: Templates, Mixins and
CTFE}\label{ch31-the-d-toolkit-templates-mixins-and-ctfe}

\texttt{MuDSL.\allowbreak{}d} is a self-contained D module using Phobos.
This chapter maps the established C++ toolkit to D and introduces the
language-specific API. The shared facilities introduced in Chapter 30
have focused tutorials in Chapters 32--36.

\section{Build and import}\label{ch31-build-and-import}

Keep \texttt{MuDSL.\allowbreak{}d} on the import path and supply the
module to the compiler:

\begin{code}
# From the MuDSL directory, with the user's app.d alongside the module:
ldc2 app.d MuDSL.d -of=app
dmd app.d MuDSL.d -of=app
gdc app.d MuDSL.d -o app
\end{code}

For an application in another directory, add the module's directory to
\texttt{-I}. The CMake installation includes the D source module. Its
C++ \texttt{INTERFACE} target exports C++ usage requirements; D
compilation is driven by the D compiler invocation above.

\begin{code}
import MuDSL;
\end{code}

\section{Compose features with a
mixin}\label{ch31-compose-features-with-a-mixin}

\begin{code}
struct MathDSL
{
    mixin DSL!(Pipeline, Operators, AST, ExprTemplates);
    double val;
    double expr_value() const { return val; }
}
\end{code}

The mixin adds selected methods directly to the enclosing aggregate.
Features must be unique. \texttt{DSLFeatures} records the selected
types; \texttt{HasFeature!(\allowbreak{}T,\allowbreak{} F)\allowbreak{}}
queries that list. The convenience predicates are \texttt{Pipeable!T},
\texttt{ExprLike!T}, \texttt{HasLiterals!T}, and \texttt{Rewritable!T}.

